      {
        "id": 235912,
        "name": "Dr_Flem",
        "username": "Dr_Flem",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/8797f3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2021-03-10T06:18:00.153Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hello, approaching my first session and I have some doubts.</p>\n<p>First: it seems to me comic characters spend a lot of times piloting aircrafts. Avengers fly on their Quinjet, the GotG fly (and destroy) a wide range of spaceships, etc.<br>\nI am unable to find a suitable quality for challenges that involve piloting, but before going and making a new one I wanted to check if someone has solved the problem in another way. Maybe using a mix of Alertness and Technology?</p>\n<p>Same with the “hotshot pilot” background. I have tried adventurer and military but they don’t seem to fit. I am thinking Hal Jordan here, and military seems more Steve Trevor, while adventurer is more suited to an Indiana Jones type.<br>\nMaybe a mix of the two?</p>\n<p>Any idea from more experienced players?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-03-10T06:18:00.153Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 3,
        "reads": 33,
        "readers_count": 32,
        "score": 21.6,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 28265,
        "topic_slug": "pilots-and-piloting",
        "display_username": "Dr_Flem",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
